          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 6 — Pressure, Winds, Storms, and Cyclones"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.893,
            0.03,
            0.917,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "89"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.083,
            0.744,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "becomes warmer and lighter. Hence, it rises, creating an area of low pressure. The air from the high pressure region of the sea blows to the low pressure region which develops on the land, resulting in a sea breeze. At night, the water is warmer than the land. Therefore, a low pressure area develops above the sea. As a result, wind blows from the land to the sea, giving rise to land breeze. Thus, the phenomenon of land breeze and sea breeze is mainly due to the pressure differences over the land and the sea."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.242,
            0.743,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we could measure the speed of the escaping air in Activity 6.5, we would find that the speed of the air is higher if the pressure difference is higher."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.306,
            0.28,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.12,
                0.306,
                0.28,
                0.4
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.288,
            0.324,
            0.539,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I have read that high-speed winds can blow off roofs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.576,
            0.337,
            0.716,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I wonder how?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.427,
            0.7,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.4 High-Speed Winds Result in Lowering of Air Pressure"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.51,
            0.488,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 6.6: Let us observe"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.548,
            0.502,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Take two balloons of the same size."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.571,
            0.592,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Inflate both balloons and tie strings to them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.593,
            0.604,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Hang the two balloons from a stick, leaving a gap of 6–10 cm (Fig. 6.13)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.634,
            0.603,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Now, blow air into the narrow space between the balloons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.678,
            0.604,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z What happens to the balloons? Note down your observations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.629,
            0.52,
            0.922,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.629,
                0.52,
                0.922,
                0.716
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.613,
                0.723,
                0.934,
                0.74
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.13: Blowing between two balloons"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.723,
            0.461,
            0.743
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Now blow harder and observe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.748,
            0.746,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When you blow between the two balloons, you observe that they move towards each other. This happens because when you blow air between the balloons, a low pressure area is created between them. The higher air pressure surrounding the balloon pushes them towards each other. You must have observed that blowing harder increases the speed at which the balloons approach each other. What can you infer from this activity? We infer that high speed winds are accompanied by a reduced air pressure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
